WEBVTT

00:00:03.180 --> 00:00:11.980
Intrigue in the Bakumatsu

00:00:26.200 --> 00:00:29.840
Tsukikage kooru daichi wo

00:00:29.840 --> 00:00:33.670
Korogari fumiwakete yuku

00:00:33.670 --> 00:00:40.880
Horobi to saisei no jidai ga hajimaru

00:00:40.880 --> 00:00:44.550
Jiyuu wo omoku kakagete

00:00:44.550 --> 00:00:48.120
Michinaki michi wo erande

00:00:48.120 --> 00:00:55.230
Mahiru yori mabushii nichibotsu wo koete

00:00:55.230 --> 00:01:02.230
Yume wo kataru you ni toki no fune wa yuku

00:01:02.230 --> 00:01:11.340
Sono yamiji no mukou ni atarashii yoake

00:01:12.110 --> 00:01:19.250
Bokura wa kitto kurayami no kaina kara umarete kita

00:01:19.250 --> 00:01:22.790
Kanawanu koi wo suruyou ni

00:01:22.790 --> 00:01:26.760
Hikari e to samayotteku

00:01:26.760 --> 00:01:32.000
Doko made mo hateshino nai kono michi wo

00:01:32.000 --> 00:01:37.490
Kaeru sube wa nai

00:01:55.850 --> 00:01:58.380
It is the third month, in the
second year of the Meiji era.

00:01:58.690 --> 00:02:02.290
The New Government Army prepares
to send out its newest ship, the Stonewall,

00:02:02.290 --> 00:02:07.820
to fight the Ezo Republic,
now occupying Goryokaku Fort.

00:02:11.040 --> 00:02:19.610
The ironclad Stonewall, later to become known as
the Kotetsu, is literally covered in steel plates.

00:02:12.300 --> 00:02:17.680
Ironclad Battleship Stonewall (Kotetsu)

00:02:19.610 --> 00:02:24.280
Even the main cannon of the Kaiyo
could not penetrate her armor.

00:02:24.520 --> 00:02:28.650
With her power, she is capable of
bringing the war to an end.

00:02:33.290 --> 00:02:36.860
About three months before...

00:02:34.000 --> 00:02:38.060
Hakodate Port

00:02:39.660 --> 00:02:42.930
After all the troubles I went
through to get to Ezo,

00:02:42.930 --> 00:02:45.400
Tayu has been spending
all her time with the master.

00:02:45.400 --> 00:02:47.910
I haven't seen the leader at all, either.

00:02:47.910 --> 00:02:49.710
Unlike the booming economy of this place,

00:02:49.710 --> 00:02:51.970
it looks like our end-of-the-year
is going to be lame.

00:02:54.380 --> 00:02:56.880
Hey, this one is bigger!

00:02:56.880 --> 00:02:59.110
I saw more over there, too!

00:02:59.380 --> 00:03:00.350
You're right!

00:03:01.350 --> 00:03:03.010
What are they doing?

00:03:03.360 --> 00:03:04.950
Hey, hey.

00:03:05.520 --> 00:03:06.960
Look what we've found!

00:03:08.830 --> 00:03:11.730
These are bullets!

00:03:12.160 --> 00:03:14.650
What? Let me see it!

00:03:14.900 --> 00:03:16.160
Get rid of them!

00:03:20.040 --> 00:03:21.800
But we found them!

00:03:22.110 --> 00:03:24.540
Kids shouldn't be playing with those.

00:03:27.650 --> 00:03:29.980
But at any rate...

00:03:29.980 --> 00:03:35.520
It's hard to believe that this place may
soon turn into a battlefield.

00:03:35.520 --> 00:03:44.390
It's been a while since the Gatling incident.

00:03:40.630 --> 00:03:44.390
Yokohama

00:03:45.100 --> 00:03:48.030
It's too bad that the Kaiyo was sunk.

00:03:48.400 --> 00:03:53.030
It took a lot of work to get
the Gatling cannon on board.

00:03:48.400 --> 00:03:51.710
Aomori Government Staff Officer Ryosuke Kuroda

00:03:53.610 --> 00:03:56.570
For the rest of my life, I'll never forget
what you've done for us.

00:03:59.110 --> 00:04:03.550
Don't worry. The boatman and the oarman
are my comrades, too.

00:04:04.220 --> 00:04:06.690
I bet no one would have thought

00:04:06.690 --> 00:04:11.120
the Republic's Minister of the Navy
and the General of the Punitive Force

00:04:06.690 --> 00:04:10.850
Ezo Republic Minister of Navy Ikunosuke Arai

00:04:11.120 --> 00:04:13.520
would be having a secret meeting
at a place like this.

00:04:13.990 --> 00:04:17.760
Kuroda, what exactly is this thing that would
bring such an enormous benefit to our republic,

00:04:17.760 --> 00:04:20.200
of which you wrote in the confidential letter?

00:04:24.270 --> 00:04:28.100
Don't be hasty. We've still got time.

00:04:31.310 --> 00:04:33.950
When Ieyasu Tokugawa
established his Shogunate,

00:04:33.950 --> 00:04:39.320
he believed the Shimazu and Mouri families
would eventually defeat the Tokugawa family.

00:04:39.320 --> 00:04:41.380
So he later confined them to the west.

00:04:41.790 --> 00:04:48.720
250 years later, the Satsuma and Choshu have
joined forces and his prediction became reality.

00:04:49.330 --> 00:04:52.560
However, the reason why the Satsuma
helped overthrow the Shogunate

00:04:52.560 --> 00:04:55.600
wasn't to exact revenge for the
Battle of Sekigahara.

00:04:55.600 --> 00:04:59.830
Rather, they cling passionately
to the ideal of a fledgling nation!

00:05:00.870 --> 00:05:03.170
However, the Choshu are different.

00:05:03.910 --> 00:05:08.810
All they care about is exercising their power.

00:05:09.510 --> 00:05:17.750
In essence, the government we established is
simply another dictatorship run by the Choshu.

00:05:19.490 --> 00:05:22.050
I no longer feel an attachment to such a place.

00:05:23.460 --> 00:05:24.500
So you're saying...

00:05:24.500 --> 00:05:28.590
Don't you think your Ezo Republic would
wish to have this Ryosuke Kuroda on its side?

00:05:28.900 --> 00:05:29.830
What?!

00:05:30.040 --> 00:05:34.900
I'm sure you've already heard what the
new government has been saying about me.

00:05:35.170 --> 00:05:36.730
And, one more thing...

00:05:38.140 --> 00:05:40.340
I've got a huge gift for you.

00:05:43.050 --> 00:05:45.210
Th-this is...

00:05:46.050 --> 00:05:47.350
Magnificent!

00:05:47.350 --> 00:05:50.620
What do you think? You can't tell me
that you don't want it.

00:05:57.330 --> 00:05:59.990
Tokyo Castle (Formally Known as Edo Castle)

00:06:04.470 --> 00:06:09.460
I'm a lucky man to be able to see you at the
very beginning of the new year, Lord Shoten!

00:06:10.040 --> 00:06:12.010
Hey, bring sake! Sake!

00:06:12.380 --> 00:06:15.070
Katsu, is this really the place
for official business?

00:06:16.110 --> 00:06:19.050
The New Year doesn't care about
whether it's official business or not!

00:06:19.050 --> 00:06:21.420
It looks like you're doing well as always.

00:06:21.750 --> 00:06:24.850
Well, it's been a long time.

00:06:25.290 --> 00:06:26.950
Yes, a long time...

00:06:27.360 --> 00:06:32.260
It appears that things aren't going so smoothly
even with the two of you working together.

00:06:33.230 --> 00:06:35.600
Even in the old days, things tend to go that way

00:06:35.600 --> 00:06:38.500
whenever you try to do things
by avoiding unnecessary bloodshed.

00:06:38.740 --> 00:06:44.870
I'm still impressed with how hard he worked
to make the Bloodless Handover possible.

00:06:45.140 --> 00:06:48.540
But it looks like we've done everything we could.

00:06:48.880 --> 00:06:53.040
We were just laughing about how
we both look aged all of a sudden.

00:06:53.250 --> 00:07:00.090
You two look aged? I guess I need
to hurry up and go to Heaven.

00:07:00.390 --> 00:07:02.090
Surely, you joke...

00:07:03.230 --> 00:07:07.390
Well actually... I have a favor
to ask of you before I die.

00:07:11.200 --> 00:07:14.600
It must have something to do with Yojiro.

00:07:15.410 --> 00:07:19.710
The Head must be sealed no matter what.

00:07:20.010 --> 00:07:24.410
Even if it is your dear comrade
it possesses, Katsu!

00:07:26.080 --> 00:07:27.450
That time...

00:07:28.290 --> 00:07:31.310
The Head chose neither me nor Saigo.

00:07:31.460 --> 00:07:35.720
This feels like having a grudge against
a girl who's not interested in me.

00:07:36.160 --> 00:07:40.830
It's fortunate that calamity
hasn't befallen either of you.

00:07:41.500 --> 00:07:47.930
However, if we continue to do nothing about the
Head, inevitably the war will spread to Tokyo!

00:07:48.140 --> 00:07:50.070
So what did you want to ask us?

00:07:50.440 --> 00:07:55.450
I'd like to ask the two of you to get him to Ezo...

00:07:55.450 --> 00:07:56.910
...the Eternal Assassin.

00:08:00.150 --> 00:08:05.610
I don't think I'm capable of that
right now. Maybe Saigo...

00:08:08.990 --> 00:08:10.820
Understood.

00:08:14.770 --> 00:08:17.960
I wonder if Yojiro can manage...

00:08:18.540 --> 00:08:24.270
Either way, Yojiro is about to face
his moment of truth.

00:08:24.940 --> 00:08:26.470
Miyako Village (Mutsunokuni)

00:08:31.720 --> 00:08:33.550
There, there, don't cry.

00:08:33.550 --> 00:08:35.610
Big Sister is going to sing a song for you.

00:08:37.320 --> 00:08:43.490
Mittsu, misora ga akeru koro
Three. Around the time when the beautiful sky opens up

00:08:39.290 --> 00:08:42.830
Hakodate Hospital

00:08:45.530 --> 00:08:52.490
Yottsu, yonaki no ko wo oute
Four. Holding a child who cries the night away

00:08:53.540 --> 00:09:00.640
ltsutsu, itsumade tsukeba yoi
Five. By when should I get there?

00:09:01.850 --> 00:09:08.950
Muttsu, mukae ni konu haha ni
Six. Mother has yet to come get me

00:09:10.050 --> 00:09:17.150
Nanatsu, naisho de urami goto
Seven. I secretly curse

00:09:18.530 --> 00:09:25.590
Yattsu, yamanba konu uchi ni
Eight. Before the old mountain witch comes

00:09:27.110 --> 00:09:34.510
Kokonotsu, ko wo sute yama koete
Nine. Abandon the baby and cross the mountain

00:09:35.950 --> 00:09:43.320
To de oni go ni narimashita
Ten. I became a little devil...

00:09:44.090 --> 00:09:47.550
O Pitiable Eternal Assassin.

00:09:48.060 --> 00:09:54.900
Because you don't know your own destiny,
you let destiny kill you.

00:10:11.950 --> 00:10:14.210
So you're Akizuki?

00:10:15.220 --> 00:10:16.690
Do you know me?

00:10:17.290 --> 00:10:21.520
You're Ryosuke Kuroda, commander
of the punitive forces against Ezo.

00:10:22.660 --> 00:10:26.530
You'll board the Stonewall with me.

00:10:26.800 --> 00:10:30.500
I'll surrender to the Republic
and offer Stonewall as a souvenir.

00:10:30.640 --> 00:10:33.430
I was asked to bring you aboard.

00:10:33.910 --> 00:10:37.930
You must be a hell of a swordsman.
Show me what you've got!

00:10:38.540 --> 00:10:41.140
I can challenge you with this if you want.

00:10:49.620 --> 00:10:53.250
It's just a joke! There would be
no part for you to play.

00:10:53.760 --> 00:10:57.990
All you need to do is watch me and
the Stonewall change history!

00:11:06.200 --> 00:11:08.730
Third month, Meiji 2, at Goryokaku in Hakodate

00:11:14.510 --> 00:11:15.600
Open the gate!

00:11:16.510 --> 00:11:18.220
What?

00:11:18.220 --> 00:11:20.710
Kuroda is going to surrender with the Stonewall?

00:11:21.020 --> 00:11:22.580
Is that true?

00:11:23.250 --> 00:11:24.080
Right.

00:11:24.720 --> 00:11:27.060
That's something I heard directly from him.

00:11:25.320 --> 00:11:28.490
Captain of the Banryu
\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\hBankichi Matsuoka

00:11:26.860 --> 00:11:29.890
Captain of the Kaiten
\h\h\h\h\hGengo Koda

00:11:27.060 --> 00:11:32.800
I asked around and confirmed that he has a
terrible reputation within the new government.

00:11:31.530 --> 00:11:34.570
Captain of the Koga
\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\hSetsuzo Furukawa

00:11:32.530 --> 00:11:35.570
Vice Minister of the Republic
\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\hTaro Matsudaira

00:11:33.100 --> 00:11:35.960
Besides, the Gatling cannons on the Kaiyo...

00:11:36.470 --> 00:11:40.300
They were taken from
the Stonewall in Yokohama.

00:11:41.070 --> 00:11:45.510
It was Kuroda who arranged
everything behind the scenes!

00:11:45.910 --> 00:11:47.010
I see.

00:11:47.010 --> 00:11:50.110
Just in case he changes his mind,

00:11:50.110 --> 00:11:55.480
I've arranged to meet him with three ships in
Miyako Bay, where the handover will take place.

00:11:56.220 --> 00:11:58.990
This way, we would avoid any damage to the
Republic in case conflict breaks out.

00:11:56.620 --> 00:12:01.230
Minister of the Army Keisuke Otori

00:11:58.990 --> 00:12:05.030
He's from Satsuma. I suppose he couldn't
stomach the new Choshu-run government.

00:12:05.360 --> 00:12:08.870
But if he comes to the Republic...

00:12:08.870 --> 00:12:12.900
Arai, your post as Minister of Navy
will be taken away.

00:12:12.900 --> 00:12:15.370
I'm already aware of such a thing.

00:12:15.370 --> 00:12:19.370
But if that's what it takes for us to get
our hands on the Stonewall!

00:12:19.910 --> 00:12:24.350
It's true... we could regain control
of the sea with the Stonewall.

00:12:24.920 --> 00:12:27.150
No, that's not all.

00:12:27.620 --> 00:12:30.250
Things could be even more interesting.

00:12:30.250 --> 00:12:31.410
What do you mean by that?

00:12:32.160 --> 00:12:35.680
Stealing the Stonewall is a serious undertaking.

00:12:35.890 --> 00:12:39.890
There's no way he would be able to
pull something like that off by himself.

00:12:40.160 --> 00:12:40.890
Meaning...

00:12:41.200 --> 00:12:44.190
Someone ordered Kuroda to do it.

00:12:45.440 --> 00:12:47.900
Could it be Saigo of the Satsuma?!

00:12:49.240 --> 00:12:51.810
What would happen if the Republic,
in the farthest north,

00:12:51.810 --> 00:12:56.750
and the Satsuma, in the
farthest south, join forces?

00:12:57.280 --> 00:12:59.720
I see. Most interesting.

00:13:00.250 --> 00:13:02.690
Japan will change hands once again!

00:13:05.260 --> 00:13:06.820
Wait a second.

00:13:06.820 --> 00:13:08.990
This sounds too good to be true.

00:13:09.330 --> 00:13:10.920
Too good to be true?

00:13:11.500 --> 00:13:16.660
Gentlemen, I understand that you want to
act swiftly, but let's calm ourselves.

00:13:17.370 --> 00:13:21.700
It is obvious that they'll start
attacking us in spring.

00:13:21.970 --> 00:13:25.970
It's not a good idea to split our forces now.

00:13:26.310 --> 00:13:28.470
That's true. This could be a trap, too.

00:13:28.780 --> 00:13:29.800
But!

00:13:29.950 --> 00:13:34.910
If that's the case, the fleet we send out
to meet them will be exposed to cannon fire.

00:13:35.150 --> 00:13:38.320
Are any of you ready to make that commitment?

00:13:42.690 --> 00:13:43.660
I'll go.

00:13:45.700 --> 00:13:47.490
It shouldn't be a problem if I go.

00:13:49.700 --> 00:13:57.300
Now that we've lost Kaiyo, our remaining ships
are not good enough to withstand their attacks.

00:13:57.640 --> 00:13:59.970
Let's take that gamble.

00:14:00.780 --> 00:14:01.350
Hijikata!

00:14:01.350 --> 00:14:04.940
Of course I'll take the lead.

00:14:43.690 --> 00:14:46.990
Miyako Bay, Morning of the 25th day of the third month, Meiji 2

00:14:54.000 --> 00:14:56.030
Everyone!

00:14:56.030 --> 00:15:01.040
A new chapter of history is about to be
written here in Miyako Bay.

00:15:01.040 --> 00:15:02.570
Give it all you've got!

00:15:02.570 --> 00:15:03.340
Yes, sir!

00:15:03.340 --> 00:15:04.240
They're here!

00:15:06.780 --> 00:15:08.610
I only see two ships.

00:15:09.210 --> 00:15:10.310
Where's the other one?

00:15:10.310 --> 00:15:12.340
I can only confirm those two!

00:15:12.920 --> 00:15:14.710
It's supposed to be three ships...

00:15:15.450 --> 00:15:17.650
I confirm only those two as well!

00:15:21.630 --> 00:15:25.660
The Satsuma Soldier Nakagoro Togo
(Also later known as Alliance Fleet
Commander Heihachiro Togo)

00:15:25.660 --> 00:15:29.860
They're finally here.
Now I'll just have to wait for the sign.

00:15:45.120 --> 00:15:47.110
Don't worry about us if something happens.

00:15:48.450 --> 00:15:49.920
Understood.

00:15:57.500 --> 00:15:58.390
I'm Hijikata.

00:15:58.730 --> 00:16:02.030
Well, well, well, the Republic's
Assistant Minister of the Army.

00:16:02.030 --> 00:16:06.470
Or should I say Shinsengumi Vice-Commander,
Toshizo Hijikata-dono.

00:16:07.100 --> 00:16:11.610
Thank you for coming so far.
I'm honored to meet you.

00:16:11.610 --> 00:16:13.640
I'm Ryosuke Kuroda.

00:16:13.640 --> 00:16:16.610
As promised we've come
to receive the Stonewall.

00:16:17.150 --> 00:16:23.990
We're prepared to receive all of you.
Come to the Republic with no worries.

00:16:23.990 --> 00:16:30.450
I appreciate your concerns, but I thought
you were supposed to come with three ships.

00:16:30.660 --> 00:16:34.830
We lost one to a storm on the way here.
Two should be enough.

00:16:34.830 --> 00:16:40.170
Of course. Just having you here
is more than enough, Hijikata-dono.

00:16:41.040 --> 00:16:44.270
We'll do something about
the remaining ones ourselves.

00:16:50.820 --> 00:16:51.940
That's the signal!

00:16:52.220 --> 00:16:53.380
Full speed ahead!

00:17:04.960 --> 00:17:05.830
How dare you!

00:17:05.900 --> 00:17:06.920
You tricked us!

00:17:11.140 --> 00:17:13.660
You're going to be the bait!

00:17:14.410 --> 00:17:21.210
We'll lure them into Miyako Bay and kill them all,
and my soldiers will board their ship.

00:17:21.550 --> 00:17:24.580
If we limp back to Hakodate,
pretending to be defeated,

00:17:24.580 --> 00:17:26.640
I'm sure they're going to be
less suspicious of us.

00:17:26.750 --> 00:17:28.490
Then we'll take them in one go.

00:17:28.490 --> 00:17:31.050
Oh, that's a bold strategy.

00:17:32.190 --> 00:17:35.850
But I like it. Go ahead with your plan.

00:17:39.000 --> 00:17:41.690
This is great. This is really great!

00:17:42.030 --> 00:17:42.960
You bastard!

00:17:46.170 --> 00:17:47.230
Clear the way!

00:17:51.880 --> 00:17:52.570
Fire!

00:17:57.950 --> 00:17:59.110
Fire!

00:18:00.080 --> 00:18:00.740
Fire!

00:18:04.290 --> 00:18:05.080
Koga!

00:18:07.690 --> 00:18:08.490
Fire!

00:18:19.440 --> 00:18:21.030
Noda! Otsuka!

00:18:23.310 --> 00:18:24.140
Vice-Commander!

00:18:24.780 --> 00:18:25.760
We must withdraw!

00:18:28.480 --> 00:18:30.040
Gatling cannon! Take aim!

00:18:30.410 --> 00:18:31.780
Don't you let him get away!

00:18:33.250 --> 00:18:35.410
Don't let him go! Fire!

00:18:49.270 --> 00:18:50.230
You!

00:18:52.770 --> 00:18:54.260
General, we need to get out of here!

00:18:54.970 --> 00:18:56.800
That won't be enough to sink this ship!

00:18:59.980 --> 00:19:02.970
Let me tell you one thing, though.

00:19:03.150 --> 00:19:07.210
You make sure that he reaches Ezo unharmed.

00:19:07.690 --> 00:19:14.020
I don't mean to be disrespectful, sir, but
I've spend a lot of time putting this plan together.

00:19:14.490 --> 00:19:18.890
You mean to tell me he's worth
that much, Saigo-san?

00:19:19.500 --> 00:19:20.550
He is.

00:19:21.970 --> 00:19:23.700
Just trust me.

00:19:24.670 --> 00:19:26.430
Damn...

00:19:27.610 --> 00:19:30.940
That man? Important?

00:19:32.540 --> 00:19:33.410
Shit!

00:19:40.990 --> 00:19:42.010
Don't let them get away!

00:19:51.360 --> 00:19:52.060
Furukawa!

00:19:59.740 --> 00:20:00.830
Fire!

00:20:08.910 --> 00:20:09.970
All hands! Withdraw!

00:20:10.250 --> 00:20:11.480
Withdraw!

00:20:14.050 --> 00:20:14.980
Furukawa!

00:21:08.570 --> 00:21:11.540
This is not where you're meant to die.

00:21:23.720 --> 00:21:25.990
Who would've thought you were still alive...

00:21:36.370 --> 00:21:37.530
Matsuoka!

00:21:39.670 --> 00:21:42.430
It is the 26th day of the third month, Meiji 2.

00:21:42.770 --> 00:21:47.300
The Republic flagship Kaiten links up with
the Banryu and returns to Hakodate.

00:21:50.510 --> 00:21:56.610
This is the first time Akizuki sees Ezo,
the setting of the showdown.

00:21:58.390 --> 00:22:02.350
<i>CROSSING OVER</i>
<i>THE STRAIT</i>

00:22:03.560 --> 00:22:09.330
Sono te wa ai no tsurugi

00:22:09.330 --> 00:22:18.370
Subete no hajimari no akashi

00:22:19.140 --> 00:22:25.100
Hikaru sora no hate

00:22:25.550 --> 00:22:30.320
Yume wa mada maboroshi

00:22:31.460 --> 00:22:42.070
Tsuki no akari kage ouyouni hashiru kono michi

00:22:42.070 --> 00:22:47.840
Chigireta ai no tsurugi

00:22:47.840 --> 00:23:00.080
Sashidasu saki wa ikusen no namida ga hitotsu ni nari

00:23:00.080 --> 00:23:05.890
Ashita wo kagayakaseru

00:23:05.890 --> 00:23:11.600
Kono te wa ai no tsurugi

00:23:11.600 --> 00:23:20.300
Subete no hajimari no akashi

00:23:32.760 --> 00:23:48.100
EPISODE 22
AN ENCOUNTER
IN THE NORTH

00:23:34.720 --> 00:23:36.320
I'm sure you understand that now.

00:23:36.320 --> 00:23:37.420
Master!

00:23:37.420 --> 00:23:41.430
To protect my comrade Enomoto and dedicate
yourself to building the Republic alongside him.

00:23:41.560 --> 00:23:44.900
That is the destiny that you two bear.

00:23:45.430 --> 00:23:49.800
But it seems that Yojiro Akizuki
hasn't realized it just yet.

00:23:48.100 --> 00:24:02.580
AN ENCOUNTER
IN THE NORTH

00:23:49.800 --> 00:23:51.740
Build the Republic together?

00:23:51.740 --> 00:23:57.440
That is your destiny, Kakunojo Yuyama...
to be the one who leads that man.

00:23:57.440 --> 00:24:01.280
I'm to lead Akizuki-sama?
